## Defect 1 — soft-lock when resting upside down (MUST FIX)
Trace (Volcanic, Reef Rover, throttle pulsed 0.9 s on / 0.3 s off), one line per ~1.2 s:
  8s d=102 ang=-234° vx=84 grounded=false bodyGrounded=true RUNNING
  9s d=106 ang=-258° vx=0  grounded=false bodyGrounded=true RUNNING
 10s…31s d=106 ang≈-255° vx≈-2 grounded=false bodyGrounded=true RUNNING  (20+ seconds, never ends)
Same with Crab Crawler (ang≈-235°, stuck from 9 s to 30 s). The rover lands on its dome slowly (below the 82 px/s "Hull crushed" impact threshold in physics.js `resolveBodyContact`) and then rests inverted forever while oxygen drains. Hill Climb Racing ends the run on any pilot-head contact.
Required behaviour: keep the instant crash on hard dome impact, AND end the run with "Hull crushed" if the dome is in contact with ground/ceiling while the chassis is inverted (|angle wrapped to ±180°| > 95°) for more than 0.6 s cumulative within any 1.5 s window. Also add a fallback: if the rover is bodyGrounded, both wheels are off the ground, and |vx| < 15 for more than 2.5 s, end the run with "Stranded" (rare wedge cases). Make sure a brief dome brush during a successful flip recovery does NOT trigger this (that's why the timer exists). Flip bonuses must still work.

## Defect 2 — Volcanic Vents first vent is a guaranteed crash (MUST FIX)
Trace (Volcanic, Reef Rover, pulsed throttle): 4s x=538 ang=-15 grounded → 5s x=745 y=215 (105 px above terrain) ang=-27 airborne → 6s x=943 ang=-125 → 8s x=1121 ang=-234 lands on dome. The same happens with Crab Crawler (ang -82 at 6 s, -211 at 8 s) and with Abyss Truck (crashed at 83 m in 9 s) and with a level-6-everything Reef Rover (crashed 105 m). The vent at roughly x=650–900 (~65–90 m) launches every vehicle ~100+ px into 3 s of airtime; combined with throttle-in-air pitch torque this is a backflip-and-a-half every time. Players will hit this on their first Volcanic run and die at 100 m.
Required: (a) no vent within the first 220 m of the stage; (b) reduce vent lift so the starter vehicle gets ~1.2–1.6 s of airtime, not 3 s (roughly 45–55% of current lift, tune by simulation); (c) scale vent lift up gradually with distance (e.g. ×1.0 at 220 m → ×1.5 by 1500 m); (d) the vent must not add net pitch torque by itself (lift the body and wheels equally so a rover entering level leaves level). Vents should feel like a fun boost, not a trap.

## Tuning 3 — air pitch control slightly too strong (SHOULD FIX)
Reef, full throttle held: 9s ang=-29 grounded → 10s ang=-40 airborne → 11s ang=-129 (crash). ~90° of rotation per second of held throttle in the air. Hill Climb Racing is a little gentler. Reduce airControl by about 20% and re-check that a full backflip is still achievable from a big ramp with a 2+ s hang (it must remain possible — flips are a core mechanic).

